instrument wingie
; grain — slow weather: time made elastic, the Wingie listening.
; Each scene: the left LED is what the microphones hear, the right one the place.

one minute becomes one hour
---------------------------
; PaulStretch of the room. fader1 (Mix) how far it stretches (1x .. 1000x),
; hold mode1 to stop time; fader3 (Volume) the level
the glacier is paulstretch 2
the level is vca
mic.both -> glacier
fader1 -> glacier.stretch
mode1 -> glacier.hold
glacier -> level
fader3 -> level.gain
level -> out
mic.both -> lights.left
glacier -> lights.right

slow-motion replay
------------------
; WSOLA: fader1 the speed (0 stands still, 1 as it was), keys1 the pitch on
; its own; hold mode1 to loop the tape; fader2 a mirrored corridor behind it
the replay is stretch 2 samplerate=quarter
the corridor is graindelay 3 samplerate=half
mic.both -> replay
fader1 -> replay.speed
keys1.pitch -> replay.pitch
mode1 -> replay.hold
replay -> corridor
fader2 -> corridor.feedback
replay corridor -> left
replay corridor.right -> right
mic.both -> lights.left
replay -> lights.right

shimmer corridor
----------------
; a granular delay feeding back an octave up (keys1 moves it), fader1 time,
; fader2 feedback, fader3 jitter
the corridor is graindelay 6
mic.both -> corridor
keys1.pitch -> corridor.pitch
fader1 -> corridor.time
fader2 -> corridor.feedback
fader3 -> corridor.jitter
corridor -> left
corridor.right -> right
mic.both -> lights.left
corridor -> lights.right
